+# Consulted sources
+
+- Title: Product Interoperability Matrix
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/
+  Decision: Checked target component interoperability and the published upgrade-path view before applying the pinned compatibility facts.
+
+- Title: Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1 (KB 440630)
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  Decision: Confirmed that a VCF 5.2.x estate upgrades VCF Operations first and then follows lifecycle-management workflows to VCF 9.1.
+
+- Title: VCF Upgrade Failure Due to NSX Back-in-Time Error (KB 430825)
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430825/vcf-upgrade-failure-cannot-upgrade-vcf-5.html
+  Decision: Ruled out 9.0.1 and 9.0.2 intermediate hops for the installed NSX 4.2.3.3 build and retained the supported direct 9.1 target.
+
+- Title: Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation Versions with Constituent Product Versions (KB 343944)
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/343944
+  Decision: Checked the source and target bill of materials and component-version correlation used by the architecture.
+
+- Title: Counting Cores for VMware Cloud Foundation and TiBs for vSAN (KB 313548)
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/313548
+  Decision: Applied the per-socket core licensing minimum and raw-vSAN capacity entitlement method that excludes the stretched topology.
+
+- Title: VCF API Specification 9.1
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://developer.broadcom.com/sdks/vcf-api-specification/latest/
+  Decision: Confirmed the published 9.1 VCF Installer API package and the SddcSpec contract represented by the pinned OpenAPI document.
